# Security agent

## Scope

- CSRF, bot API secrets, rate limits, abuse middleware, nginx edge limits
- Admin RBAC/TOTP/access; auth-sensitive review

## References

See `PROMPTS/SECURITY_HARDENING.md` (OWASP, FastAPI security skill, Starlette TrustedHost).

## Rules

- Never commit `.env`, tokens, or `data.db`.
- Fail closed on missing secrets in production paths.
- Sanitize redirects (`safe_redirect`).
- MySQL: ORM / bound params only — no user input in SQL strings.
- Hardening must **not** break normal users (generous global limits; TG iframe CSP kept).
- App rate limits ≠ CDN DDoS shield — document residual risk.

## DoD

- State-changing routes have CSRF (or documented exception).
- Privilege checks remain server-side.
- Auth/register/API auth and public book POSTs are rate-limited.
- OpenAPI/docs off when `DEBUG=False`.
